<title>AUSTRALIA: Australian oil, gas output rises in May vs April.</title>
<headline>Australian oil, gas output rises in May vs April.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Department of Primary Industries and Energy issued the following data for Australia's petroleum production in May:</p>
<p>		 Crude Oil  Condensate	Total    Total '000 bpd</p>
<p>			 (megalitres)</p>
<p>May 97	   2,123.2	712.0	2,835.1	  575.3</p>
<p>Apr 97	   1,984.4	608.1	2,592.4	  543.6</p>
<p>May 96	   2,254.8	556.9	2,811.7	  570.5</p>
<p>Fiscal 95/96  24,058.1    6,193.3     30,251.3	  521.3</p>
<p>Fiscal 94/95  26,795.0    4,394.5     31,189.6	  537.5</p>
<p>Percentage change on year-to-date:</p>
<p>Fiscal	     1.6	  9.9	   3.3		n/a</p>
<p>Calendar	  -4.2	 17.9	   0.1		n/a</p>
<p>	     Liquefied Petroleum Gas* Ethane	Natural Gas</p>
<p>		   (megalitres)	   (million cubic metres)</p>
<p>May 97		364.6		  16.6	   2,588.3</p>
<p>Apr 97		341.2		  15.3	   2,108.8</p>
<p>May 96		336.8		  16.3	   2,584.1</p>
<p>Fiscal 95/96    3,649.4		 186.5	  29,984.9</p>
<p>Fiscal 94/95    3,608.8		 203.0	  29,207.6</p>
<p>Percentage change on year-to-date:</p>
<p>Fiscal		 4.0		    -7.0	    -2.3</p>
<p>Calendar	     4.3		    -7.9	    -3.7</p>
<p>NOTE: * Naturally occurring LPG.</p>
<p>One megalitre = 6,290 barrels.</p>
<p>One cubic metre = 35.3 cubic feet</p>
<p>r = revised.</p>
<p>Fiscal year ends June 30.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
